Subject: [PATCH] profile: device profile loader, with hardwareConcurrency

Adds the loader for the profile, the JSON the browser is launched with.
It is read from the command line on first use, so every process sees it
from startup, and each getter falls back to the host's real value when
the profile leaves a field out. The first value wired through is the
core count, set at base::SysInfo::NumberOfProcessors so
navigator.hardwareConcurrency and the browser's own thread pools agree.
A claim above the host's real core count is clamped to the host, since a
page can measure it.

